+### Setting-by-Setting Technical Paragraphs
+
+- **`postgresql_rls`:** Evaluates database health via `GET /api/v1/admin/diagnostics`. Asserts that the single-head Alembic migration tree is fully applied (82/82 migrations), connection pool saturation remains under 75%, and all 100 application tables enforce `FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY`. Connection latency is sampled continuously with healthy thresholds < 15ms.
+- **`realtime_hub_outbox`:** Tracks the transactional outbox relay daemon (`database/outbox/relay.py`). Measures the unprocessed message queue depth, average dispatch lag (healthy < 5s), and PostgreSQL `LISTEN/NOTIFY` channel subscription status. Stalled outboxes trigger immediate administrative alerts.
+- **`job_worker_pool`:** Monitors asynchronous background task executors responsible for webhook dispatch, automated snapshot creation, and audit logging. Reports total active tasks, concurrency utilization, and dead-letter queue (DLQ) depth. Any non-zero DLQ count indicates unhandled job failures requiring inspection.
+- **`wasm_script_sandbox`:** Monitors the in-process Wasmtime runtime executing custom field formulas and transition helpers. Verifies compiler initialization, memory consumption caps (default 64MB per instance), and fuel budget limits preventing CPU exhaustion.
+- **`agent_runtime_providers`:** Asserts the availability and response latency of registered AI model providers (`gemini`, `openai`, `ollama`). Reports monthly token consumption against configured budget ceilings, warning administrators before cloud budget caps halt automated transition gates.
+- **`remote_runner_fleet`:** Tracks external execution nodes connected via mutual TLS (mTLS) over dedicated port `:8444`. Reports active runner counts, certificate expiration dates, and heartbeat timestamps. Runners failing to report within 30 seconds are marked offline and their active leases rescheduled.
+- **`rate_limiter`:** Reports the runtime state of in-memory token bucket rate limiters across public and authenticated routes. Tracks blocked request volumes and active IP throttle mappings, ensuring system resilience against abusive traffic.
+- **`realtime_pubsub_probe` and `websocket_ws_probe`:** On-demand latency probes. The pub/sub probe (`POST /api/v1/admin/diagnostics/probes/realtime`) injects a synthetic outbox notification and captures `LISTEN/NOTIFY` roundtrip time (typically ~0.38ms). The WebSocket probe initiates a live `/ws` binary ping frame in the operator's browser, measuring connection setup (~13.7ms) and ping/pong roundtrip latency (~0.44ms).
+
+---
+
+## 14. Universal Object Graph Link Auditor Studio
+The Universal Object Graph Link Auditor Studio (`/admin/link-auditor`) inspects, classifies, and remediates referential integrity anomalies across all registered entities.
+
+![Link Auditor Studio - Desktop Light](images/slice4-link-auditor-1440x900-light.png)
+
+
+### Link Auditor Studio Configuration Table
+
+| Field Name | What It Controls | Allowed Values / Format | Default | Security / Operational Impact |
+| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
+| `audit_scan_mode` | Graph traversal mode for detecting invalid links | `full`, `incremental` | `full` | Scans `object_links` table across all 7 defect classes |
+| `defect_class_filter` | Filters links by formal invalidity category | All 7 invalidity classes (or `ALL`) | `ALL` | Isolates specific defect patterns for forensic inspection |
+| `justification` | Mandatory operator rationale for purging links | String (Minimum 10 characters) | Required | Recorded in immutable activity ledger; rejects < 10 chars with 422 |
+| `dry_run` | Two-stage purge blast-radius simulation toggle | Boolean (`true` / `false`) | `true` | Calculates exact link deletion counts without modifying database |
+| `confirm_phrase` | Confirmation phrase required for destructive purge | Exact string `"PURGE"` | None | Prevents accidental deletion of object graph relationships |
+
+![Link Auditor Integrity Scan Active](images/slice4-link-auditor-integrity-scan-active.png)
+
+### Setting-by-Setting Technical Paragraphs
+
+- **`audit_scan_mode`:** Determines the scanning depth executed by `POST /api/v1/admin/object-links:audit`. In `full` mode, the auditor traverses the entire `object_links` table, checking foreign key validity against registered entities, workspace boundaries, and directed acyclic graph invariants without table locks.
+- **`defect_class_filter`:** Allows administrators to filter detected anomalies across the 7 formal invalidity classes:
+  1. `DANGLING_TARGET`: Target object UUID does not exist in the database.
+  2. `DANGLING_SOURCE`: Source object UUID does not exist in the database.
+  3. `EXPIRED_ENDPOINT`: One or both endpoints reference an object soft-deleted beyond the retention window.
+  4. `TENANT_MISMATCH`: Links connect entities across disjoint workspace boundaries without federation.
+  5. `TYPE_UNREGISTERED`: `link_type` is not registered in the schema registry.
+  6. `CARDINALITY_VIOLATION`: The relation violates 1:1 or 1:N cardinality constraints.
+  7. `SELF_REFERENTIAL_CYCLE`: A circular dependency violates DAG hierarchical sort order.
+- **`justification`:** The mandatory rationale string required by `POST /api/v1/admin/object-links:purge`. The string must contain at least 10 non-whitespace characters (e.g. `"Decommissioning orphaned test links post-cutover"`). Rationale strings containing fewer than 10 characters are rejected with HTTP 422.
+- **`dry_run`:** When `dry_run=true`, the purge endpoint evaluates the candidate link IDs, checks foreign key impacts, and returns a blast-radius report summarizing counts per defect class without deleting records. When `dry_run=false`, the purge executes within an atomic transaction.
+- **`confirm_phrase`:** The explicit confirmation token required during Stage 2 destructive purging. The administrator must enter the confirmation phrase `"PURGE"` in the confirmation dialog before the deletion request is dispatched.
+- **`immutable_audit_ledger`:** Every completed purge operation writes an immutable `INVALID_OBJECT_LINK_PURGED` event to `activity_records`. The record captures the operator's principal ID, timestamps, purged link IDs, defect classes, and the full justification string.
